{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (Task ID: 5479) from a code generation pipeline for the go-unix-utils project. The task is to implement srd072 requirements R4.1-R4.4 for `cmd/od` (octal dump utility). Specifically:\n   - R4.1: Must exit 0 when dump completes successfully\n   - R4.2: Must exit 1 when invalid option given or file cannot be opened\n   - R4.3: Differential tests must compare stdout and exit codes between Go binary and reference binary (`god`) via `pkg/testutils`\n   - R4.4: Tests must cover a comprehensive list of scenarios including: default octal dump, -t with each format letter (a, c, d, f, o, u, x) and size variants, -A address radix modes, -j skip bytes, -N read bytes, -w output width, -v output duplicates, traditional short options (-b, -c, -d, -o, -s, -x), multiple -t options, duplicate suppression with '*', stdin input, multi-file input, and error cases (invalid type, missing file)\n\n   The acceptance criteria require: all R4 requirements implemented, differential tests covering each R4 requirement, `go build`, `go vet`, and `go test` all pass.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: comparing Go binary output against GNU reference binary (`god` from Homebrew)\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` and `DiffTest` struct for test harness\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Exit code handling (0 for success, 1 for errors)\n   - Type specifiers for od: format letters (a, c, d, f, o, u, x) with size suffixes\n   - Address radix options (d, o, x, n)\n   - Byte range selection (-j skip, -N read limit)\n   - Output width control (-w)\n   - Duplicate suppression ('*' lines) and verbose mode (-v)\n   - Traditional short option al