rts no issues\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/od/ -count=1` and ensure all tests pass or skip gracefully\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all four relevant files (srd072-od.yaml, main.go, od_test.go, parse.go) and was about to begin implementing the R4.1-R4.4 requirements. My analysis determined that:\n   - The exit code behavior (R4.1, R4.2) is already correctly implemented in the existing code\n   - The differential test framework (R4.3) is already set up\n   - The main work needed is adding error case tests to satisfy R4.4's comprehensive coverage requirement\n   \n   The files to modify are:\n   - `cmd/od/main.go` - May need minor adjustments for exit code handling\n   - `cmd/od/od_test.go` - Needs error case tests added\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Add error case tests to `cmd/od/od_test.go` by creating an `errorCaseTests()` function that returns `[]testutils.DiffTest` with cases for invalid type strings, missing files, and invalid options. These tests should use `ExitCode: 1` and `discardStderr` normalizer. Then append these to the test list in `TestDiff`. After writing code, run `go build`, `go vet`, and `go test` to verify all acceptance criteria are met.\n\n   The task description states: \"R4.4: Tests must cover: default octal dump, -t with each format letter (a, c, d, f, o, u, x) and size variants, -A address radix modes, -j skip bytes, -N read bytes, -w output width, -v output duplicates, traditional short options (-b, -c, -d, -o, -s, -x), multiple -t options, duplicate suppression with '*', stdin input, multi-file input, and error cases (invalid type, missing file).\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5479/a1493a0d-7f60-4033-a125-2d29782fe75b.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking 